  "verbalization": "Azadiradionolide appears to have a mechanism of action that involves targeting multiple molecular entities, ultimately leading to a relationship with SMMC-7721. The evidence suggests that Azadiradionolide acts as a target for SNU-387 and Anolobine, both of which are implicated in the biological process that leads to the inhibition of SMMC-7721. The final scores from the three paths indicate a consistent and plausible relationship, with each path contributing to the overall evidence of a mechanistic link between Azadiradionolide and SMMC-7721. The shared target of SNU-387 and Anolobine, along with the direct interaction of these compounds with SMMC-7721, suggests that the observed effects are mediated through a common pathway. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that Azadiradionolide exerts its biological activity through a mechanism involving the modulation of molecular targets that ultimately result in the suppression of SMMC-7721.",
